{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@preconcurrency","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"map","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transform","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@escaping","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncSequence\/Element"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncThrowingMapSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingMapSequence"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A mapping closure. ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accepts an element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of this sequence as its parameter and returns a transformed value of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same or of a different type. ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can also throw an error, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends the transformed sequence.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"transform"}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An asynchronous sequence that contains, in order, the elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"produced by the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"text":" closure.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"text":" method to transform every element received from a base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asynchronous sequence. Typically, you use this to transform from one type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of element to another.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"text":" produces ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5"},{"text":". The closure provided to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"text":" method","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" and looks up a corresponding ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"text":" from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"romanNumeralDict"},{"text":" dictionary. This means the outer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await in"},{"text":" loop","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterates over ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"text":" instances instead of the underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"text":" produces. Also, the dictionary doesn’t provide a key for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4"},{"text":", and the closure throws an error for any key it can’t look up, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receiving this value from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"text":" ends the modified sequence with an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"error.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let romanNumeralDict: [Int: String] =","    [1: \"I\", 2: \"II\", 3: \"III\", 5: \"V\"]","","do {","    let stream = Counter(howHigh: 5)","        .map { (value) throws -> String in","            guard let roman = romanNumeralDict[value] else {","                throw MyError()","            }","            return roman","        }","    for try await numeral in stream {","        print(numeral, terminator: \" \")","    }","} catch {","    print(\"Error: \\(error)\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"I II III Error: MyError() \""]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/asynccompactmapsequence\/map(_:)-21iha"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncCompactMapSequence\/map(_:)-21iha","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"map(_:)","role":"symbol","platforms":[{"beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":fal